{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fy4ZC4o9HEsW8oc6ejdai1","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t    figure_anchor: \"ch18-zenith-instruments-answer-one-question\"\n151\t    checkpoint_after: false\n152\t\n153\t#-- §3 and §6 carry a second objective tag deliberately. Both k8s.io\n154\t#-- snapshots they rest on (resource-metrics-pipeline, logging-architecture)\n155\t#-- are tagged D2.3 in their own frontmatter, and Ch 13 owns D2.3. The dual\n156\t#-- tag is the honest record that these two sections are seams, not new\n157\t#-- territory, and it tells the question-writing stage that items drawn\n158\t#-- from them are legitimately interleaved rather than off-domain.\n159\t\n160\t# --- Skill v5.3 Part 11: Soundings pre-chapter diagnostic ---\n161\tsoundings_planned:\n162\t  question_count: 8\n163\t  topics:\n164\t    - \"probes as a yes/no signal to the kubelet, producing no history (Ch 5 §7)\"\n165\t    - \"what metrics-server is scoped to, and what it keeps no record of (Ch 13 §7)\"\n166\t    - \"why `kubectl top` fails on a cluster that is otherwise healthy (Ch 13 §7 / Ch 10 §3)\"\n167\t    - \"what 'utilization' is measured against when an autoscaler reads it (Ch 5 §8 / Ch 17 §7)\"\n168\t    - \"why log collection is a per-node job rather than a per-app one (Ch 6 §7 / Ch 13 §7)\"\n169\t    - \"why `kubectl logs` stops being able to answer a question (Ch 13 §3)\"\n170\t    - \"what one service's logs cannot tell you when a request crosses five (Ch 17 §3)\"\n171\t    - \"what a mesh sidecar can report on without the app knowing (Ch 17 §5)\"\n172\t\n173\t# --- Skill v5.3 Part 8: practice-question budget ---\n174\tquestion_budget:\n175\t  soundings: 8\n176\t  taking_your_bearings: 15             # across 3 checkpoints (5 + 5 + 5)\n177\t  practice_questions: 17\n178\t  total_this_chapter: 40\n179\t#-- B4's table says 10 Bearings. B4 also says, in the same file, that \"the\n180\t#-- 10 is a contract to exceed, not a target to hit,\" and shipped Ch 13\n181\t#-- (budgeted at 10) carries three checkpoints of six. Eight sections and\n182\t#-- three distinct arcs cannot be served by two checkpoints without leaving\n183\t#-- §4–§7 untested until the end. 15 across three, at the skill's five-per-\n184\t#-- checkpoint floor, is the smallest structure that covers the chapter.\n185\t#-- Practice stays at 17 exactly: B4's weight-proportional derivation,\n186\t#-- 15 + 2 x (5 - 4) = 17. Do not change it — the derivation reproduces the\n187\t#-- published 44/28/16/12 split to within 1.1 points and Ch 18 is one of\n188\t#-- its terms.\n189\t\n190\tkb_tags:\n191\t  objectives: [\"D4.1\"]\n192\t  concepts:\n193\t    - \"observability\"\n194\t    - \"monitoring\"\n195\t    - \"unknown-unknowns\"\n196\t    - \"instrumentation\"\n197\t    - \"telemetry\"\n198\t    - \"opentelemetry\"\n199\t    - \"signals\"\n200\t    - \"traces\"\n201\t    - \"metrics\"\n202\t    - \"logs\"\n203\t    - \"baggage\"\n204\t    - \"otel-collector\"\n205\t    - \"time-series\"\n206\t    - \"metric-labels\"\n207\t    - \"cardinality\"\n208\t    - \"metrics-server-vs-monitoring\"\n209\t    - \"utilization-relative-to-requests\"\n210\t    - \"prometheus\"\n211\t    - \"pull-model\"\n212\t    - \"scraping\"\n213\t    - \"service-discovery\"\n214\t    - \"exporters\"\n215\t    - \"client-libraries\"\n216\t    - \"pushgateway\"\n217\t    - \"promql\"\n218\t    - \"alertmanager\"\n219\t    - \"grafana\"\n220\t    - \"distributed-tracing\"\n221\t    - \"span\"\n222\t    - \"root-span\"\n223\t    - \"trace-id\"\n224\t    - \"context-propagation\"\n225\t    - \"jaeger\"\n226\t    - \"cluster-logging-architecture\"\n227\t    - \"node-level-logging-agent\"\n228\t    - \"fluentd\"\n229\t    - \"fluent-bit\"\n230\t    - \"sidecar-logging\"\n231\t    - \"log-rotation\"\n232\t    - \"reliability\"\n233\t    - \"sli\"\n234\t    - \"slo\"\n235\t    - \"sla\"\n236\t    - \"error-budget\"\n237\t    - \"four-golden-signals\"\n238\t    - \"red-method\"\n239\t    - \"use-method\"\n240\t  commands:\n241\t    - \"kubectl-top\"        #-- RETRIEVED from Ch 13 §7, not introduced here\n242\t    - \"kubectl-logs\"       #-- RETRIEVED from Ch 13 §3, not introduced here\n243\t#-- Both commands are already owned. They appear so the research stage\n244\t#-- resolves the right shards; they are not this chapter's teaching surface.\n245\t#-- PromQL is a query language, not a kubectl verb, and is deliberately not\n246\t#-- listed here — §4 teaches that it exists and what it is for, not syntax.\n247\t\n248\tfigures_planned:\n249\t  - \"ch18-fig01-monitoring-vs-observability\"\n250\t  - \"ch18-fig02-otel-four-signals\"\n251\t  - \"ch18-fig03-trace-spans-across-services\"\n252\t  - \"ch18-fig04-prometheus-pull-architecture\"\n253\t  - \"ch18-fig05-sli-slo-golden-signals\"\n254\t  - \"ch18-fig06-cluster-logging-architectures\"   #-- ADDED beyond B3's list\n255\t  - \"ch18-zenith-instruments-answer-one-question\"\n256\t---\n257\t````\n258\t\n259\t# Chapter 18 Outline — Reading the Instruments\n260\t\n261\t## Chapter-type note (read first)\n262\t\n263\t`content`. Full contract applies: witty subtitle, Attention Budget, epigraph, Soundings, Why This Chapter Matters, What You'll Learn, ≥2 Taking Your Bearings, Exam Alert + Practice Questions, Chapter Summary, The Voyage Ahead. One Zenith illustration, exactly one, at §8.\n264\t\n265\tTwo chapter-level facts the drafting stage must not lose:\n266\t\n267\t- **The metadata line carries 12%, not 5%.** See the frontmatter comment. This is the third chapter in a row to make this ruling and the first two shipped honoring it.\n268\t- **This is the last content chapter.** The Voyage Ahead hands off to Ch 19 (synthesis), not to more material. Its job is to close Domain 4 and turn the reader toward review — B3 sets retrieval at the 25% ceiling here precisely because everything after this point is assessment.\n269\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82977d3f-dade-46ff-8162-aa1f979ee266","u