{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LLv7AWKtBe5wc5o8PacwxW","type":"tool_result","content":"46\t> \"Baggage allows you to propagate arbitrary key-value pairs.\"\n47\t\n48\t## Drafting note for §5\n49\t\n50\t\"Arbitrarily distributed across process and network boundaries\" is the sourced sentence that closes\n51\tthe loop shipped Ch 17 opened (\"Break a monolith into microservices and one request becomes\n52\ttwenty\"). The Service A / Service B sentence is concrete enough to carry the mechanism without a\n53\tcode sample, which matters because B1 rates D4 recall-and-recognition and §5 must not drift into\n54\timplementation.\n55\t\n56\tW3C TraceContext is **not** exam surface at KCNA level. Name it at most once; do not grade it.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82977d3f-dade-46ff-8162-aa1f979ee266","uuid":"45a95554-4571-4338-91c3-ad1d0e754deb","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:08:08.112Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\opentelemetry-context-propagation-2026-08-31.md","content":"> \"Baggage allows you to propagate arbitrary key-value pairs.\"\n\n## Drafting note for §5\n\n\"Arbitrarily distributed across process and network boundaries\" is the sourced sentence that closes\nthe loop shipped Ch 17 opened (\"Break a monolith into microservices and one request becomes\ntwenty\"). The Service A / Service B sentence is concrete enough to carry the mechanism without a\ncode sample, which matters because B1 rates D4 recall-and-recognition and §5 must not drift into\nimplementation.\n\nW3C TraceContext is **not** exam surface at KCNA level. Name it at most once; do not grade it.\n","numLines":12,"startLine":46,"totalLines":57}}}
