{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxwX6q1wPYiCF1LAcHue6E","type":"tool_result","content":"705:=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/absent-component-pattern.md ===\n706-\n707-## Chapter 17 update (2026-08-31) — the fifth instance, and a WORDING RULING\n708-\n709-Chapter 17 §7 fires the pattern at the VerticalPodAutoscaler: the VPA object can be\n710-created on a cluster where no VPA is installed, and nothing acts on it. Same shape as\n711-an Ingress with no controller and `kubectl top` with no metrics-server, one layer over.\n712-See [[vertical-pod-autoscaler]].\n713-\n714-## ⚑⚑ THREE PHRASINGS ARE LIVE IN SHIPPED TEXT. Do not \"fix\" Ch 17 in isolation.\n715-\n716-  Variant A  \"an object without its component does nothing\"\n717-             ch 3 x2, ch 10 x12, ch 11 x4  = 18. The ★ Fixed Point, and inside a\n718-             graded Ch 11 Practice option.\n719-  Variant B  \"the object exists; nothing happens without the component\"\n720-             ch 13 x3 (:300, :1279, :1281); ch 17 §7; AND the B7 ledger row :339.\n721-  Variant C  \"the object exists BUT nothing happens without the component\"\n722-             ch 6 x2 (:1005, :1082); AND B3 retrieval-architecture.md's own summary.\n723-\n724-The integration report for Ch 17 states that Chapter 13 never retrieves this pattern\n725-and that Ch 17 is the last chance. That is measurably wrong — Ch 13 retrieves it three\n726-times, in Variant B, which is exactly what Ch 17 uses and exactly what the binding\n727-ledger specifies.\n728-\n729-RECOMMEND standardizing on VARIANT A and correcting B3, B7, Ch 6, Ch 13 and Ch 17\n730-together. Do not single out Chapter 17.\n731-\n732-## ⚠ ATTRIBUTION — this one IS a Ch 17 error and should be fixed now\n733-\n--\n1354:=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/cloud-native-characteristics.md ===\n1355-# Concept: The five characteristics of cloud native systems\n1356-\n1357-## ★ Fixed Point (verbatim — do not reword)\n1358-\n1359-**Cloud native is characterized by loosely coupled systems that interoperate in a manner\n1360-that is secure, resilient, manageable, sustainable, and observable.**\n1361-\n1362-[source: cncf-cloud-native-definition-2026-08-23]\n1363-\n1364-## The structure matters as much as the list\n1365-\n1366-Five characteristics ATTACHED TO loosely coupled systems — not five characteristics\n1367-floating free. The loose coupling is the spine; the five are what a loosely coupled\n1368-system must manage to be worth having.\n1369-\n1370-| Characteristic | What it costs you to skip |\n1371-|---|---|\n1372-| Secure | verification at every boundary, not just the edge |\n1373-| Resilient | survives the loss of any one part |\n1374-| Manageable | changeable without rebuilding it |\n1375-| Sustainable | affordable to keep running, in people and in power |\n1376-| Observable | you can ask it what it is doing, and it will answer |\n1377-\n1378-## ⚠ The two most-dropped items\n1379-\n1380-\"Sustainable\" and \"observable\" are what distinguish this list from a generic\n1381-software-quality list, and they are the two candidates most often drop. Practice Q1's\n1382-distractor D is built precisely on that."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82977d3f-dade-46ff-8162-aa1f979ee266","uuid":"7961a88e-569a-40a3-a404-08a196c1e8a5","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:09:31.451Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"705:=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/absent-component-pattern.md ===\n706-\n707-## Chapter 17 update (2026-08-31) — the fifth instance, and a WORDING RULING\n708-\n709-Chapter 17 §7 fires the pattern at the VerticalPodAutoscaler: the VPA object can be\n710-created on a cluster where no VPA is installed, and nothing acts on it. Same shape as\n711-an Ingress with no controller and `kubectl top` with no metrics-server, one layer over.\n712-See [[vertical-pod-autoscaler]].\n713-\n714-## ⚑⚑ THREE PHRASINGS ARE LIVE IN SHIPPED TEXT. Do not \"fix\" Ch 17 in isolation.\n715-\n716-  Variant A  \"an object without its component does nothing\"\n717-             ch 3 x2, ch 10 x12, ch 11 x4  = 18. The ★ Fixed Point, and inside a\n718-             graded Ch 11 Practice option.\n719-  Variant B  \"the object exists; nothing happens without the component\"\n720-             ch 13 x3 (:300, :1279, :1281); ch 17 §7; AND the B7 ledger row :339.\n721-  Variant C  \"the object exists BUT nothing happens without the component\"\n722-             ch 6 x2 (:1005, :1082); AND B3 retrieval-architecture.md's own summary.\n723-\n724-The integration report for Ch 17 states that Chapter 13 never retrieves this pattern\n725-and that Ch 17 is the last chance. That is measurably wrong — Ch 13 retrieves it three\n726-times, in Variant B, which is exactly what Ch 17 uses and exactly what the binding\n727-ledger specifies.\n728-\n729-RECOMMEND standardizing on VARIANT A and correcting B3, B7, Ch 6, Ch 13 and Ch 17\n730-together. Do not single out Chapter 17.\n731-\n732-## ⚠ ATTRIBUTION — this one IS a Ch 17 error and should be fixed now\n733-\n--\n1354:=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/cloud-native-characteristics.md ===\n1355-# Concept: The five characteristics of cloud native systems\n1356-\n1357-## ★ Fixed Point (verbatim — do not reword)\n1358-\n1359-**Cloud native is characterized by loosely coupled systems that interoperate in a manner\n1360-that is secure, resilient, manageable, sustainable, and observable.**\n1361-\n1362-[source: cncf-cloud-native-definition-2026-08-23]\n1363-\n1364-## The structure matters as much as the list\n1365-\n1366-Five characteristics ATTACHED TO loosely coupled systems — not five characteristics\n1367-floating free. The loose coupling is the spine; the five are what a loosely coupled\n1368-system must manage to be worth having.\n1369-\n1370-| Characteristic | What it costs you to skip |\n1371-|---|---|\n1372-| Secure | verification at every boundary, not just the edge |\n1373-| Resilient | survives the loss of any one part |\n1374-| Manageable | changeable without rebuilding it |\n1375-| Sustainable | affordable to keep running, in people and in power |\n1376-| Observable | you can ask it what it is doing, and it will answer |\n1377-\n1378-## ⚠ The two most-dropped items\n1379-\n1380-\"Sustainable\" and \"observable\" are what distinguish this list from a generic\n1381-software-quality list, and they are the two candidates most often drop. Practice Q1's\n1382-distractor D is built precisely on that.","numLines":59,"totalLines":59}}
